TO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRATA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HYODO, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOYAMA, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURODA, ISAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGASHIMA, YUKIHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A light-colored glass having high transmittance which contains 0.02 % or more and less than 0.06 %, in terms of Fe2O3 as a colorant, of total iron oxide, less than 0.024 % of FeO and 0 to 0.5 % of cerium oxide, has a composition wherein the ratio of the amount of FeO in terms of Fe2O3 to that of total iron oxide is less than 40 %, and has, in the case of a thickness of 3.2 mm, a transmittance of solar radiation of 87.5 % or more and a transmittance of visible light by C source of 90 % or more; and a glass plate with an electrically conductive film comprising said glass and a transparent, electrically conductive film formed on the surface thereof.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne du verre clair à facteur de transmission élevé, qui contient 0,02 % ou plus et moins de 0,06 %, en termes de Fe2O3 en tant que colorant, d'un total d'oxyde de fer, moins de 0,024 % de FeO et 0 à 0,5 % d'oxyde de cérium. Ledit verre présente une composition dont le rapport entre la quantité de FeO en termes de Fe2O3, et le total d'oxyde de fer est inférieur à 40 %, et comporte, lorsque son épaisseur est de 3,2 mm, un facteur de transmission du rayonnement solaire de 87,5 % ou plus et un facteur de transmission de la lumière visible provenant d'une source C, de 90 % ou plus. L'invention porte également sur une plaque de verre à couche électro-conductrice, comprenant ledit verre, et sur une couche transparente et électro-conductrice formée sur la surface de ce dernier.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>